=============================================================================== -->
<section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-14">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Where you can chat</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-readable text-slate-600">
    Both work the same way. The only difference is what we have to ask you for.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="card border-t-4 border-t-telegram">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
        <span class="text-2xl" aria-hidden="true">✈️</span>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">Telegram</h3>
        <span class="badge bg-sky-100 text-sky-800">Most private</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
        You open a link, press START, and we are chatting. We never learn your phone
        number — not even a scrambled one, until you press START.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card border-t-4 border-t-whatsapp">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
        <span class="text-2xl" aria-hidden="true">💬</span>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold">WhatsApp</h3>
        <span class="badge bg-green-100 text-green-800">Most familiar</span>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
        The app most people already have. We need your number so we can message you
        there. It is scrambled before it is stored and never kept in readable form.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">
    We can also text you reminders if you ask — but you cannot chat with us by text.
  </p>
</section>

<!-- ===== What this is / privacy =================================================== -->
<section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-white">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-14">
    <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-14">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">What this is, and what it is not</h2>

        <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <p>
            <strong class="text-ink">It is a research prototype.</strong>
            It is being built and tested as part of an MSc project. It is not a medical
            service and has not been approved as one.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-ink">It is not a doctor.</strong>
            It does not give diagnoses and it will never tell you which medicine to take
            or how much.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-ink">It covers mothers and babies in the first year.</strong>
            Postpartum mothers, and infants from birth to 12 months. For anyone else, it
            will say so and point you to a health worker.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-ink">It errs on the side of caution.</strong>
            If it is unsure, it will tell you to get seen. That is deliberate.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Your privacy</h2>

        <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
          <p>
            <strong class="text-ink">We ask for as little as possible.</strong>
            A name to call you. Nothing else is required.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-ink">Telegram needs no phone number at all.</strong>
            We only ever ask for one if you choose WhatsApp, because that is the only way
            to reach you there.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-ink">Numbers are scrambled before they are stored.</strong>
            They are never kept in a form anyone can read back.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-ink">Conversations are stored anonymously</strong>
            so the system can be checked and improved. You will be asked before anything is
            kept.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-6">
          <a href="/privacy" class="link">Read the full privacy notice</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

